Z||000000||85ZainoGT||10-09-2001||09:47 PM||||I went to autozone to buy dome lights, but the one the book says to fit doesnt work..  help?  and also, are there any other interior lights that I am missing?<P>------------------<BR>Paul Ventimiglia<BR>1985 White/Silver GT <BR>2.8L 4 Speed LOADED :)<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sigpic2529_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||My7Fieros||10-10-2001||01:36 AM||||Do what I do....go to a hardware store and buy bulbs for Malibu outdoor lighting...they come in packs of two or six I believe. Take one of the original bulbs from your car to match up..you'll see. They're the EXACT same thing only a good bit brighter (also you can get diff colors if you want). Thats all I use...(btw thats for the 4 lights above  between the sunvisors).<BR>Other bulbs (the little bitty ones) are under the shifter console...one for the PRND12 (automatics only), and one on each side (outer side) of the ashtrays. Some Fieros have a light by your feet...one on the drivers side and one on the pass side...Ive never had to change those so Im not sure what kind those are..prob the same as the Malibu ones...<P>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="blue"><B><I>My 7 Fieros</FONT></FONT></B></I><P>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 10-10-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by My7Fieros (edited 10-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||stsmithgt||10-10-2001||09:49 AM||||Hmmmmmmm....? Malibu lighting?  Sounds like a good accent. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  The bulbs down by the kick panel are the bigger bulbs I think like the malibus your talking about.||||reg||5
